  "observations": [
    "Completed canonical HTTP Session decisions now project the exact durable CID/SID into the existing Core and install its staged participant coordinator while retaining the original Store command writer. The current actor is revalidated and must match the fenced projection; its ordinary canonical principal supplies the installation tenant. There is no reacquired authority fence, fabricated Device or native physical-peer admission.",
    "The shared project_session_container helper is used by both HTTP and actual signed attachment. It refuses stopped runtime, terminal Session and absent actor; Core preserves its existing external projection origin and terminal tombstones. Replays ensure the checked coordinator exists without replacing it. This reuses existing project_external_session and attach_peer_session support; no new managed Session origin, upstream patch, schema or public wire field is needed.",
    "The direct Service test inspects the actual Core Session: empty Participants/Connections, zero pending/admitted capacity and no physical peers. Its checked coordinator begins at revision1 and replay preserves that revision. The actual HTTP SDK fixture creates/invites and accepts without native peers or media, then an actual signed native peer replays the same invitation and attaches to that one Session. HTTP end retires it; HTTP and signed older invitation replay retain the original receipt without recreating the Core.",
    "The other2general Session cases preserve four-party shared HTTP/signed receipts and actual physical peer retirement. Service27, server66serial, public9 and privateAI caller/context/return/restart1 pass on the final unchanged source. This qualifies the empty shared-container prerequisite, not physical initial SIP, telephone provider mapping or general availability."
